module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses" as NonEmptyStr,
  // FOUND ON THE LADDER, read from execution and not from prose: the failure occurs as a located
  // TypeError at evaluation, which is Mitigatable. The row's own DISTINGUISHING FACTS receipt already
  // said FOUND AT MITIGATABLE; this is the first time the typed field carries it. Read for the
  // source-to-interpretation path only -- see the INT-KERNEL REFINEMENT receipt for what was and was
  // not executed, and the PR body for the per-path statement.
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "eval_cast's arms derive from std.coercion rows, one table read by both layers, so no cast outside the checker's decision reaches a runtime refusal"
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an explicit `as` cast the typechecker Accepts but the evaluator refuses, so what the cast admits has two authorities (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority): v1.compiler.infer validate_cast abstains whenever either side is outside std.coercion dag_cast_rules, and the seed interpreter's eval_cast decides the cast alone at runtime. HARM: a checked program crashes on a construct its checker blessed, which is below the section 4b floor.",
    "SPECIMENS: `n as Nat` in console_size_of_stat (then in gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_diagnostic_bundle, now gunbc.host.boot_attempt after cut 4d-ii) aborted an mtcollins1 boot diagnostic with `TypeError: cannot cast Int to Nat` (CI run 35871654468) although the value was guarded by `n < 0`; runner_microvm_cell_readiness_store decode_attempt hit the same class earlier. The sweep at the fix found three more unguarded Int-as-Nat sites (gunbc.ci_workflow_scan_producer scan walk bound, gunbc.harness.harness_cli harness_release_cli ceiling and generation).",
    "RESOLUTION FOR Int -> Nat: it is a REFINEMENT cast, not a re-typing, because a total meaning would have to clamp a negative, which std.checked_arithmetic already names as the section 5 absorbing fallback. std.coercion refinement_cast_rules is the one authority: validate_cast refuses a cast over one of its rows at compile time, eval_cast refuses the same rows as an unreachable echo, and std.checked_arithmetic checked_int_to_nat (promoted from retired gunbc.spark.serving_load_probe (deleted #13779)) is the sanctioned crossing. A nonnegative literal needs no cast and a Nat-typed value casts by identity.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the defect is a checker/evaluator disagreement on cast admission, not a spelling mismatch on an identity cast (identity_cast_compares_type_spellings) and not a missing refusal at the checker alone. FOUND AT MITIGATABLE (a located runtime TypeError). NOW, for refinement_cast_rules rows: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED on the source-to-interpretation path. `Bool as Int` is no longer a dag_cast_rules row (a `Bool -> Bool` identity keeps Bool in the cast domain), so validate_cast refuses it at compile time. Two companions landed with it, read from the same rows: std.coercion dag_subtraction_refinement types a difference of refinement values at the row's source type (zero, one or many rows: many refuses), so `(a - b) as Nat` over two Nats is a refinement cast rather than an identity; and std.algebra count / length return Nat. RESIDUE, stated rather than claimed away: a cast outside the dag_cast_rules domain is still decided by eval alone; the IMPLICIT grounded Int -> Nat identity (grounded_primitive_coproduct_identities) still admits an unproven Int in a Nat return, argument or field position with no check -- its wall is staged next, measured at identity grain before it lands. CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED -- cast admission is decidable. NEXT TRIGGER: eval_cast's arms derive from std.coercion rows (one table read by both layers) so no cast outside the checker's decision reaches a runtime refusal.",
    "KERNEL INTO TEXT, CLOSED AT THE CHECKER (operator ruling via stern-bat-401, 2026-10-24). `n as String` over a kernel Int (and Nat, Bool, Float, Unit) sat in the residue above: String is outside dag_cast_rules, so validate_cast abstained, the interpreter rendered the value, and the Rust emitter fabricated `panic!(\"unsupported cast from i64 to String\")` (three arms in gunbc.durable_cas_file_store, measured by wise-wolf-174 on the rfm-rung-census route). v1.compiler.infer host_text_source_reading is now the one reading of whether a source has an implicit route into host text, and non_text_kernel_cast_into_text_diags refuses its kernel arm into every target text_representation_by_identity classifies as text. The sites are fixed forward through std.integer int_to_decimal_string and std.nat nat_to_decimal_string, chosen by the source type the refusal names (std.algebra length returns Int). RESIDUE: a non-kernel, non-nominal source outside dag_cast_rules is still decided by eval alone, and an Unidentified text target is unjudged (gunbc.rung_drop text_boundary_identity_wall).",
    "THE EMITTED ROUTE HAS THE SAME DISAGREEMENT (recorded at #14769's rework, 2026-10-25): v1.compiler.emit emit_typed_cast_shared ends in an unsupported-cast abort (emit_error_expr), reached by any cast the checker abstained on and no emit route realizes. A user-declared type spelled Nat, cast `as Int`, is skipped by validate_cast when its source is outside the cast domain and aborts there at runtime. The trigger is the one this row already implies: every `as` without a declared route refuses at type check. A corpus cast census is not a prerequisite (retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`); this does not establish corpus-wide coverage); the change uses scoped review and focused tests.",
    "INT-KERNEL REFINEMENT, THE SAME DISAGREEMENT WITH NO ARM (PR #16211, 2026-11-10). `1 as IpmiChannelNumber` (IpmiChannelNumber = `Int where range(min: 0, max: 15)`, dag/extdeps/bmc/ipmi_channel.dag:42) is admitted by the checker with NO diagnostic at all and refused by the evaluator, so two authorities decide one cast. MEASURED as a differential inside one closure against an identity-cast control, never as an absolute count: the in-range cast adds no row, the out-of-range literal `16 as` adds exactly one BLOCKING TypeMismatch, and a non-literal Int adds only the advisory WhereRefinementUnenforced -- identical for IpmiUserId (1..63) and Port (1..65535), so it is the class and not one type (claim_batch 079745a9, invocation efc3a04c). HARM: the only two sites that ever wrote it, gunbc.machine_intake.host_interface_inventory::mtjade1_bmc_link_reading and gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_platform_observation::mtcollins1_dedicated_bmc_lan_reading, RESOLVE and then die with TypeError { msg: `cannot cast Int to IpmiChannelNumber` }, and no CI path evaluates either module, which is why both stood broken; test.claim.machine_intake.host_interface_segment_anchor_witness was 0/5 for the same reason. THE CLASS IS NOT FIXED BY THIS ROW: it has live inhabitants elsewhere on main, test.claim.serving.router_proxy_config_witness 1 PASS / 8 FAIL on `cannot cast Int to Port` at both 8732750e2d69 (invocation 3d6e6fb0) and 2e02a8bcbeee (260e039f), and Port is declared in std (dag/std/types.dag:286), so the narrower reading -- that only brands declared outside std fail -- is refuted. Three further production inhabitants are inventoried in that PR: 503 as HttpStatus and 2000 as Milliseconds in gunbc.serving.router_proxy_config (unobserved, masked by the Port refusal upstream of them in the same witness) and `t as EpochSecs` in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate::belt_exit_spool_stage_times, whose only production route is the workflow_dispatch-gated operator job named at gunbc.ci.ci_spec::gunbc_ci_rlm_launch_deployment_receipt_target and which needs a real host exec, so no hermetic claim can reach that arm. MECHANISM, so the next reader need not re-read the seed: in src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs, fn eval_cast at :14647 matches the target name against exactly three arms at :14691 and every other target falls to `t => Err(refused(&val, t))` at :14709, while its String case is the one arm that walks the target kernel -- a range-refined alias over the Int kernel therefore has no arm to land on. The emitted route was fixed for representation-identical refinement in gunbc#10266 (test.claim.emitter_nested_refinement_cast_witness), so the interpreter is now the layer that disagrees with both the checker and the emitter. RESOLVED AT THE SITES, NOT AT THE ROOT: the corpus builds every other range-refined Int value with a bare literal (gunbc.machine_intake.mtjade1_factory_network::mtjade1_factory_segment_prefix, gunbc.spark.fabric_rail_desired::fabric_rail_prefix_length), and the wall in test.claim.long.where_refinement_enforcement_witness checks an int literal against the target predicate at record fields, returns, data inits, call args and as-casts alike, so #16211 drops the cast. DISCRIMINATED, not asserted: at base the two reading rows plus the six anchor and ethernet rows above are FAIL on that one verbatim TypeError and at head every one of them is PASS, with no row moving the other way and test.claim.machine_intake.oob_power_action_witness 15/15 on both legs (claim_batch 2421cd4c / 98228682, invocations efba81c7 and ce9e2982); the bare out-of-range `channel: 16` is still refused and the bare in-range literal still evaluates, measured at both layers (claim_batch 13988100 / 8d39f8fc, invocations 0e974c65 and 7d2f43bc). WHY NOT THE TWO WIDER FIXES: making eval_cast admit an Int into a refined alias would create an IMPLICIT route against section 4 and would silently admit 16, because a non-literal at a refined position is advisory only; and a refinement_cast_rules row per refined target is a language-layer ruling, not a pull request -- it collides with 29,157 authored `as NonEmptyStr` occurrences, 2,358 `as PciDeviceId` and 3,332 `as Sha256DigestHex`. The class fix is the trigger above, dispatched as its own lane by silent-bee-845 on 2026-11-10 with this receipt's inventory as its population and the EpochSecs checked constructor as its first PR, because that is the site on an operator-run job.",
    "THE ARM LANDED (PR #16224, 2026-11-10). validate_cast (src/v1/04_infer.dag) now refuses, as a blocking RefinementCastRefused (a typed CompilerDiagnostic variant added to v1.std.core; NOT InternalError, whose variant is reserved for a compiler fault -- a refusal of user source must name its own reason, DESIGN gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed), a cast whose TARGET carries an int-literal refinement predicate and whose SOURCE is Int/Nat-kernel and not the target itself: subject `invalid cast: <Src> as <Tgt> is a refinement cast, not a re-typing`. eval_cast is untouched, so both layers now refuse the same shape and the checker/evaluator fork is CLOSED for the numeric int-refinement source-to-interpretation path. Executed at the heal mirror head 796f58b9 (the mirror carries int_refinement_cast_domain; base main eefe616d), census invocation 8166330c: `1 as IpmiChannelNumber` and a call source cast into a DIFFERENT refined carrier (`pc() as IpmiUserId`) each add one blocking row of the arm's class (RefinementCastRefused); an identity cast onto its own carrier (`pc() as IpmiChannelNumber`) and a widening `pc() as Int` add none (both layers admit them); the out-of-range wall and the identity rows stay additive (ipmi witness 7/7). NON-RESOLVED sources reach neither the arm nor a silent fork: a Divergent source is refused by the realization check (CastRealizationRefused, nameless carrier) and a TypeVariable source is not authorable (the checker refuses field access on an unconstrained T first), so the wildcard on the arm's InferredNode admits no eval-refused cast on this path. The literal casts this class named were dropped to bare in-range literals (router_proxy_config `503`/`2000`, the Port and GitTreeEntryNameAfterSlashValue test casts); router_proxy_config_witness went 1/9 to 9/9 and no other witness row moved (claim_batch head 57 PASS / 7 pre-existing FAIL invocation 9d52608d vs base 49/15 invocation c5494d24). The ipmi row that had DOCUMENTED the fork is re-pinned as the positive control for the refusal, per its own comment. RESIDUE this arm does NOT close, stated not claimed away: a target refined by a NON-int predicate (NonEmptyStr over Str, PciDeviceId/Sha256DigestHex over Text) keeps eval_cast's kernel gate, because a String source is outside the arm's Int-kernel domain and refusing it there would open the OPPOSITE fork; the implicit grounded Int to Nat identity wall and casts outside the dag_cast_rules domain stay eval-decided. The rung stays Read at Mitigatable / BelowCeiling: this arm closes ONE sub-population by compile-time refusal but does NOT build the rung's stated trigger (eval_cast deriving from the same std.coercion table as the checker), so a cast outside the checker's decision can still reach a runtime refusal. V2 GENERALIZATION (6b, should generalize but not now): the v2 checker src/v2/compiler/infer.dag has its OWN validate_cast and its OWN CompilerDiagnostic but NO CastRealizationRefused, so whether it carries this same checker-vs-evaluator fork is UNKNOWN until read -- the v2 seed was not run here and this receipt makes no claim about it. Trigger and follow-up: once a v2 witness shows the fork red, v2's validate_cast gains the int-refinement arm with its OWN typed variant. Named, not claimed, not done here.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
